<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chahar Mongols</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chahars</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chahar are a Mongol people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-mongolia">Inner Mongolia</a>. In the 16th century they formed one of the six <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tumen">tumens</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dayan-khan">Dayan Khan</a>'s restored Mongol realm and were the personal following of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a>. Their ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ligdan-khan">Ligdan Khan</a> tried to reunite the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> by force in the 1620s but was driven west by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchus</a>, and in 1635 his son submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-taiji">Hong Taiji</a>, bringing the Chahar into the Qing state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chahar-mongols.jpg" alt="Chahar Mongols" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Esiymbro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mongol_Subgroups_Chakhar_1911.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
